<title>UK: SDX Business Systems shares set premium.</title>
<headline>SDX Business Systems shares set premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in telephone systems group SDX Business Systems Plc set a premium on their first day of trade on London Stock Exchange on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The shares closed at 172-1/2p with 4.2 million shares traded, after being placed at 160p with institutional shareholders.</p>
<p>The issue valued SDX at 56.8 million stg and raised 7.1 million stg net, which will be used to cut borrowing and to redeem preference shares.</p>
<p>The float was sponsored by Kleinwort Benson.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 745</p>
</text>
